WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.069 --> 00:00:02.702
-Our next guest
is a talented actress

00:00:02.702 --> 00:00:04.536
you know from shows like
"How I Met Your Mother"

00:00:04.536 --> 00:00:05.705
and "The Avengers" films.

00:00:05.705 --> 00:00:07.273
She stars as Ann Coulter
in the limited series

00:00:07.273 --> 00:00:09.408
"Impeachment:
American Crime Story,"

00:00:09.408 --> 00:00:12.011
which airs Tuesdays only on FX.
Let's take a look.

00:00:12.011 --> 00:00:14.413
-George, we're celebrating.

00:00:14.413 --> 00:00:17.750
These tapes are going to be
in the Smithsonian one day.

00:00:17.750 --> 00:00:20.552
We're living a page
in a U.S. history book!

00:00:20.552 --> 00:00:23.523
-I'm just saying maybe we
should hold off on celebrating

00:00:23.523 --> 00:00:26.159
until we know for sure there's
something usable on those tapes.

00:00:26.159 --> 00:00:28.961
-This is a coup d'etat,
and we're the coup.

00:00:28.961 --> 00:00:30.996
Do you know how rare that is?

00:00:30.996 --> 00:00:32.731
If there was ever a night
to crack open something

00:00:32.731 --> 00:00:35.401
[bleep] decent, it's now.

00:00:35.401 --> 00:00:37.170
We're starting.

00:00:37.170 --> 00:00:39.806
♪♪

00:00:39.806 --> 00:00:41.707
-Please welcome back
to the show our friend

00:00:41.707 --> 00:00:43.409
Cobie Smulders, everyone!

00:00:43.409 --> 00:00:45.111
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:45.111 --> 00:00:46.846
Cobie.

00:00:46.846 --> 00:00:50.449
-Hey, buddy.
-Cobie, I just want to say.

00:00:50.449 --> 00:00:54.587
It is an excellent -- You have
an excellent Ann Coulter.

00:00:54.587 --> 00:00:57.756
-Oh. Thank you, thank you.

00:00:57.756 --> 00:01:00.193
It's been a journey, my friend.

00:01:00.193 --> 00:01:01.861
-Do you find
it's an effective voice

00:01:01.861 --> 00:01:04.531
to use around the house
with your husband and children?

00:01:04.531 --> 00:01:08.434
-Oh, gosh. I wouldn't bring it
anywhere near Taran, but --

00:01:08.434 --> 00:01:12.605
Um, I will say,
when I was in production,

00:01:12.605 --> 00:01:14.807
I would read to my daughters

00:01:14.807 --> 00:01:16.976
a lot at night
with the Ann Coulter voice.

00:01:16.976 --> 00:01:20.079
And I would always ask first
because it already

00:01:20.079 --> 00:01:24.050
makes every character
in the book really sarcastic.

00:01:24.050 --> 00:01:25.518
[ Laughter ]

00:01:25.518 --> 00:01:28.220
Which -- You don't find a lot
of really sarcastic characters

00:01:28.220 --> 00:01:30.890
in children's books.
You know, you'd be surprised.

00:01:30.890 --> 00:01:33.592
Um, but, yeah,
I'd be reading like...

00:01:33.592 --> 00:01:35.528
[as Coulter]
"He would climb up her trunk

00:01:35.528 --> 00:01:38.898
and swing from her branches
and eat her apples."

00:01:38.898 --> 00:01:40.566
[ Laughter ]

00:01:40.566 --> 00:01:42.001
And they'd be like,

00:01:42.001 --> 00:01:44.504
"Mom, can we go back
to your voice, please?"

00:01:44.504 --> 00:01:46.505
[ Laughter ]

00:01:46.505 --> 00:01:48.708
-You had helped --
You were helping out,

00:01:48.708 --> 00:01:51.477
I should say, with some
child care, not your children.

00:01:51.477 --> 00:01:55.582
You have three new nieces,
nephews. What are they?

00:01:55.582 --> 00:01:59.519
-I have two new nieces
and two new nephews,

00:01:59.519 --> 00:02:02.488
but there is a set of triplets
in there.

00:02:02.488 --> 00:02:05.658
So, I was just up in Canada.
There they are!

00:02:05.658 --> 00:02:07.693
-It's kind of stunning.

00:02:07.693 --> 00:02:09.228
I know triplets exist,

00:02:09.228 --> 00:02:11.864
but it's really stunning
to see them all at once.

00:02:11.864 --> 00:02:13.566
-And it's really something else

00:02:13.566 --> 00:02:15.267
to try to hold them all
in your lap.

00:02:15.267 --> 00:02:17.637
I mean, that was
a terrifying moment for me.

00:02:17.637 --> 00:02:20.340
But, yeah, so it's like
every family member

00:02:20.340 --> 00:02:22.041
decided to have babies
at the same time,

00:02:22.041 --> 00:02:24.244
and my brother
really outdid everyone.

00:02:24.244 --> 00:02:27.447
-Yeah. I know your husband,
Taran Killam,

00:02:27.447 --> 00:02:29.782
to be someone
who is highly invested

00:02:29.782 --> 00:02:31.750
in the holiday of Halloween.

00:02:31.750 --> 00:02:34.720
He is a man
who loves a good costume.

00:02:34.720 --> 00:02:37.257
Do you share this passion?

00:02:37.257 --> 00:02:41.060
-You know, um,
they say opposites attract.

00:02:41.060 --> 00:02:43.596
And that'd be our case.

00:02:43.596 --> 00:02:48.968
I literally have nothing.
I have no costume.

00:02:48.968 --> 00:02:51.504
My husband is set.
Our kids are set.

00:02:51.504 --> 00:02:54.741
You can see our house
from outer space.

00:02:54.741 --> 00:02:57.810
It has so many lights on it.

00:02:57.810 --> 00:03:00.813
But I am like -- I think
the other day, I was like,

00:03:00.813 --> 00:03:02.348
"I know what I'll be!

00:03:02.348 --> 00:03:04.350
We got a kitten
a couple months ago.

00:03:04.350 --> 00:03:08.621
I'll be a crazy cat lady!
That makes sense!"

00:03:08.621 --> 00:03:12.091
And my whole family is like,
"Okay, Mom."

00:03:12.091 --> 00:03:15.127
-Do you feel like the children
resent you for not taking it

00:03:15.127 --> 00:03:16.963
as seriously as Taran,
or do you think they're fine?

00:03:16.963 --> 00:03:19.966
-I mean, I think they resent me
for a lot more,

00:03:19.966 --> 00:03:23.769
but I think we could
put it on the list for sure.

00:03:23.769 --> 00:03:28.541
Um, yeah, so, I mean,
I'm more about, like,

00:03:28.541 --> 00:03:30.743
I'm going to help you
get that candy.

00:03:30.743 --> 00:03:32.912
I'm going to chart the route.

00:03:32.912 --> 00:03:37.149
I'm going to tell you beforehand
what to grab out of that bowl

00:03:37.149 --> 00:03:39.885
if you show up at the door
and there's just a bowl there.

00:03:39.885 --> 00:03:42.922
We're going to
strategize together.

00:03:42.922 --> 00:03:44.958
Am I going to look like me

00:03:44.958 --> 00:03:49.795
with maybe, you know, a funky
little cat ears on my head?

00:03:49.795 --> 00:03:51.363
That's what we have to do.

00:03:51.363 --> 00:03:53.099
What's more important?

00:03:53.099 --> 00:03:55.134
-They will learn to value that
as they get older.

00:03:55.134 --> 00:03:57.203
And I think once they hit
their mid to late teens,

00:03:57.203 --> 00:03:58.971
they're going to really hate
Taran for taking it

00:03:58.971 --> 00:04:00.139
so seriously.
-You're right.

00:04:00.139 --> 00:04:01.974
Really being imaginative
and creative.

00:04:01.974 --> 00:04:04.610
I think so. I think so.
That's my hope.

00:04:04.610 --> 00:04:07.946
-Um, Taran is also
in "Impeachment."

00:04:07.946 --> 00:04:10.115
And I would imagine
one of the most fun things

00:04:10.115 --> 00:04:12.485
about doing a show like this
is getting to sit back

00:04:12.485 --> 00:04:16.389
and watch the other wonderful
performances by this great cast.

00:04:16.389 --> 00:04:18.624
-Yeah, for sure.

00:04:18.624 --> 00:04:20.859
He actually got hired
on the project first.

00:04:20.859 --> 00:04:24.797
And because of him,
I was able --

00:04:24.797 --> 00:04:26.866
He felt the tone of the set,

00:04:26.866 --> 00:04:29.168
and he was having
such a great time.

00:04:29.168 --> 00:04:30.736
The crew was amazing
on this one,

00:04:30.736 --> 00:04:34.207
and he was having such a blast
that it made me not,

00:04:34.207 --> 00:04:37.676
you know, totally terrified
to play Ann Coulter.

00:04:37.676 --> 00:04:40.746
Um, he -- It was a little bit
more exciting after that.

00:04:40.746 --> 00:04:42.448
We didn't have
any scenes together,

00:04:42.448 --> 00:04:45.017
but I think that our scenes
sometimes line up

00:04:45.017 --> 00:04:48.054
where his scene ends
and then I'm in the next one,

00:04:48.054 --> 00:04:51.357
which is interesting
and new for us.

00:04:51.357 --> 00:04:53.759
-What was it like
growing up in Canada

00:04:53.759 --> 00:04:55.161
while this was all going down?

00:04:55.161 --> 00:04:58.430
Was the impeachment scandal
and drama something

00:04:58.430 --> 00:05:02.134
that you were all watching
the same way we were here?

00:05:02.134 --> 00:05:05.704
-I mean, we certainly got
the news up north, for sure,

00:05:05.704 --> 00:05:08.374
but I was, you know,

00:05:08.374 --> 00:05:11.910
16, 17 and very self-involved.

00:05:11.910 --> 00:05:15.481
And so I was just
kind of focused on,

00:05:15.481 --> 00:05:18.918
you know, my own stuff.

00:05:18.918 --> 00:05:20.819
But I do remember broad strokes.

00:05:20.819 --> 00:05:24.624
I do remember -- A lot of it
is actually "SNL" sketches.

00:05:24.624 --> 00:05:27.559
I mean, a lot of those
kind of jokey references

00:05:27.559 --> 00:05:29.028
I definitely --

00:05:29.028 --> 00:05:30.896
-A deeply unfortunate way
to learn history.

00:05:30.896 --> 00:05:32.197
It should be noted.

00:05:32.197 --> 00:05:35.168
-Absolutely. Somewhat
inaccurate. Somewhat inaccurate.

00:05:35.168 --> 00:05:40.106
Um, but, so I did know
sort of the moments,

00:05:40.106 --> 00:05:41.908
but it has been an education.

00:05:41.908 --> 00:05:46.245
And I'm in -- You know, I'm not
in every one of these episodes,

00:05:46.245 --> 00:05:48.848
so I'm kind of learning
as I go a lot

00:05:48.848 --> 00:05:51.851
and also did a lot of research
beforehand.

00:05:51.851 --> 00:05:53.753
So it was like --
I learned a lot about

00:05:53.753 --> 00:05:56.221
this time in history, so...

00:05:56.221 --> 00:05:58.524
-Do you get to keep the wig
at least?

00:05:58.524 --> 00:06:00.292
It's a very iconic wig.

00:06:00.292 --> 00:06:01.827
-Oh, I mean, it would have been
at least something

00:06:01.827 --> 00:06:03.762
for Halloween, yeah.

00:06:03.762 --> 00:06:05.998
Um, no, no, I didn't.

00:06:05.998 --> 00:06:10.035
That wig -- There was so much
work done for that look.

00:06:10.035 --> 00:06:12.604
It was, like,
a prized possession

00:06:12.604 --> 00:06:14.073
of that hair department.

00:06:14.073 --> 00:06:15.641
So, no, I didn't get to keep it.

00:06:15.641 --> 00:06:17.376
-I got to be honest.
If I was a neighborhood kid

00:06:17.376 --> 00:06:20.345
and I knew you to be an integral
part of the Marvel Universe,

00:06:20.345 --> 00:06:25.084
I'd be pretty bummed out if you
walked out as weird cat lady.

00:06:25.084 --> 00:06:26.786
-Okay.
We got to get some spandex.

00:06:26.786 --> 00:06:29.021
We got to figure it out.
-Just something.

00:06:29.021 --> 00:06:31.623
Just some effort.
-It's coming.

00:06:31.623 --> 00:06:33.592
-It's always wonderful
to see you.

00:06:33.592 --> 00:06:36.228
Loved your family,
and I look forward to next time.

00:06:36.228 --> 00:06:37.897
-Definitely, Seth. Take care.

00:06:37.897 --> 00:06:40.098
-"Impeachment:
American Crime Story"

00:06:40.098 --> 00:06:41.901
airs Tuesdays only on FX.

